# Only debhelper is listed. The Rust toolchain is not taken from the archive:
# trixie ships rustc 1.85 but the crate is built against whatever stable
# rustup installs in the release container, and an archive-wide build-dep on
# "cargo" would pin the package to one release's toolchain. Build with
# "dpkg-buildpackage -d" so dpkg-checkbuilddeps does not object to a cargo
# that is on PATH but not dpkg-installed; see README.Debian.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/Alacrity-Education/Stencicrity

Package: stencicrity
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xdg-utils
Description: merge KiCad solder-paste gerbers into one stencil order
 Stencicrity takes the gerber exports of several KiCad projects and lays every
 board side out on a single stencil sheet, so that a batch of small boards can
 be ordered as one stencil instead of one stencil per project.
 .
 It copies all paste openings over, marks the border of every board with
 dotted lines so the sheet can be cut apart afterwards, and places dowel-pin
 holes on a fixed grid so that every cut-out piece fits the same fixture
 plate. The result is a single F_Paste gerber, packed in a zip together with a
 copper reference layer, that a stencil house cuts like any other.
 .
 Copper pads that have no paste opening in the source - test points, jumper
 pads, connectors soldered by hand - are collected and presented in a terminal
 interface, where each of them is either opened or left closed. The decisions
 are stored in a plain text file next to the gerbers, so a second run over the
 same boards needs no interaction.
 .
 This package ships a single statically linked Rust binary; apart from the C
 runtime it pulls nothing in at run time.
